    "restoration_notes": "One of the flagship species for productive forest restoration in the Amazon. Organic cacao agroforestry simultaneously restores biodiversity while generating sustainable income. Native shade trees improve soil fertility, microclimate, pollination, and natural pest regulation. Highly suitable for restoring degraded cattle pastures. Organic certification substantially increases value addition and producer resilience. Strong cooperative governance (CAMPPAX) demonstrates an effective restoration business model. FYNOS AI should prioritize cacao as a cornerstone species for integrated restoration landscapes combining ecological recovery, carbon sequestration, biodiversity conservation, and sustainable livelihoods."
